g built and must keep working; a launcher WITH no readable application.ini is a build about to run unpinned and raises. (3) THE RESIDUE SWEEP HAD ALMOST NO REACH -- not blocked on, and the sharpest of the three. Exempting home/.config wholesale hid 108 files behind an argument that only ever applied to two named entries, so nothing appearing anywhere under that root could be residue. Both are now named, .config/pulse (1 file) and .config/libreoffice (107), and a new directory under .config is residue again, driven red by a new fixture. home/.cache stays wholesale for one file whose name embeds the machine's own id, and the cost is now enumerated rather than gestured at: eight files, three in the font library's cache, four in the GL driver's, one loose. The green's REACH is stated where the artifact's reader meets it -- what could still fail the check (a write at the top of the sandbox HOME, a new directory under .config, a new top-level entry in the arena, anything outside it) and what could not (a new file inside .cache) -- because a green a reader will over-trust is worse than a not-run. THE PORT DEVIATION IS RECORDED AS A DEVIATION rather than defended as not-one, at the lane lead's direction and as a standing question for the author about the contract's letter: extensions.zotero.httpServer.port moves off the shipped 23119 (build/defaults/preferences/zotero.js:172), the ratified text forbids a non-default option with no carve-out for one that does not touch the feature under test, and three adapters landed tonight carrying this same deviation from one lane briefing -- so it is one question, not three judgment calls. Beside the admission: why (four instances share the machine and a port collision makes the target fail to start, which the layer would read as a defect of the target); what it could have moved, in a form a reader can CHECK from the committed artifacts rather than take on trust (no assertion that ran against any adapter on this roster reads anything through an HTTP port, since check_local_by_default needs configure and status, the model-cache clause needs install, query and status, and every adapter that could have reached a port declares query and status absent); and the alternative that removes it (one instance at a time on the shipped port, strictly more faithful, costing serialization across lanes, which a single-lane run should prefer). DECISIONS.md untouched. Three smaller corrections, each of the kind this repo punishes: the profile carries 36 preferences in 45 lines and an earlier sentence called all of them preferences, the file's nine standard header comments being the difference; the install event recorded the build's absolute location, which is one machine's business where the application.ini stamp is the provenance, so bench/results/** now carries ZERO occurrences of the operator's home path across all three artifacts, achieved by moving the arena off $HOME and REGENERATING rather than by editing a committed artifact, which would have made it no longer the driver's output; and the reach paragraph first quoted a run's total file count, which the next run contradicted (1080 against 1070) -- the variation lives entirely in the toolkit's own cache, a declared root, so the exempted groups are stable at 116 and that is what the prose states, with the reader sent to the check's own created_count for a total. Four more control arms driven red against the committed tree and restored, bringing the round's total to nine: writing app.update.enabled again fails its guard; removing the unstamped-launcher refusal fails its own; re-exempting .config wholesale fails two, the exemption-shape test and the stray-under-.config sweep, the latter coming back `assert 'pass' == 'fail'`; and putting the build path back into the install event fails the artifact-hygiene guard. Verdicts unchanged across every re-run: 1 pass, 1 fail, 3 not-offered, 0 not-run.
